---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HeaderSection from '../layouts/HeaderSection.astro';
import MainContentSection from '../layouts/MainContentSection.astro';
import ThumbnailGrid from '../components/ThumbnailGrid.astro';
import Thumbnail from '../components/Thumbnail.astro';

const title = 'The instruments that I play';
const sectionClassName = 'gear';
---

<Layout
  title='Anton Emery | Gear'
  description='The instruments of Anton Emery, celtic fingerstyle guitarist'
  keywords='celtic, guitar, acoustic, sheet musc, tabs'
>
  <HeaderSection
    sectionClassName={sectionClassName}
    imagePath='/src/assets/guitar-banjo.jpg'
    altText='guitar and banjo leaning on the couch'
  />
  <MainContentSection title={title}>
    <p>
      It has been said that we live in the second golden age of guitar building,
      and I am inclined to agree. The craftsmanship and innovation in modern
      guitar making is truly remarkable. There are amazing instruments available
      today at all price points, from large production facilities to solo
      luthiers building ten guitars a year.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am lucky to own a few nice instruments, which inspire and bring me joy
      every day.
    </p>
    <h2 class='h5'>
      2008 Alberico OM, "Swannanoa" - Sitka Spruce/Indian Rosewood
    </h2>
    <p>
      This guitar is my number one. If the house was on fire I would grab this
      one first. It is made by Vancouver Island based luthier <a
        href='https://www.albericoguitar.com/'
        target='_blank'
        rel='noopener noreferrer'>Fabrizio Alberico</a
      >. It is his interpretation on the classic OM shape, being just slightly
      larger and deeper. To me this gives it a touch bigger bass tone and
      response, while still being super comfortable to play.
    </p>
    <p>
      This instrument has a Sitka spruce top, Indian Rosewood back and sides,
      and cocobolo binding and headplate. The neck is mahgony with an ebony
      fingerboard. The scale length is 25.5 inches, with a nut width of 1.75
      inches and bridge spacing of 2.25 inches. It has Gotoh 510 tuners, and a
      dual source pickup system consisting of a McIntyre Feather and DPA mic
      both wired to a stereo endpin jack.
    </p>
    <p>
      For my tastes, this is the consummate fingerstyle instrument. It is
      articulate, balanced, and responsive, with great note separation and
      clarity. One frequency does not overpower another. It has just the right
      amount of overtones. The intonation is great up and down the neck. I have
      had a few folks tell me it is the most in tune guitar they have ever
      played. The neck is a comfortable C shape.
    </p>
    <p>
      Here are some pictures of me with it over the years. It is funny to see
      the guitar when I first got it, the top was almost white. Now almost
      twenty years later it has mellowed to a deep golden color.
    </p>
    <ThumbnailGrid>
      <Thumbnail
        imagePath='/src/assets/alberico-sheet-music.jpg'
        altText='Acoustic guitar on a table with sheet music'
      />
      <Thumbnail
        imagePath='/src/assets/alberico-1.jpg'
        altText='Anton sitting on the couch with his Alberico guitar'
        caption='Photo by Fabrizio Alberico'
      />
      <Thumbnail
        imagePath='/src/assets/alberico-2.jpg'
        altText='Anton sitting on the couch with his Alberico guitar'
        caption='Photo by Fabrizio Alberico'
      />
      <Thumbnail
        imagePath='/src/assets/alberico-3.jpg'
        altText='Anton sitting outside in the sun with his Alberico guitar'
      />
      <Thumbnail
        imagePath='/src/assets/alberico-4.jpg'
        altText='Anton sitting outside in the sun with his Alberico guitar'
      />
      <Thumbnail
        imagePath='/src/assets/alberico-5.jpg'
        altText='Anton playing in the classical position'
        caption='Experimenting with different playing positions. This must have been right after I got the guitar, as the top is still very light in color.'
      />
      <Thumbnail
        imagePath='/src/assets/alberico-6.jpg'
        altText='Anton recording in the studio with his guitar.'
        caption='Recording my first album, "Noone Lasses", in Doug Youngs studio.'
      />
    </ThumbnailGrid>
  </MainContentSection>
</Layout>
